00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:05.965
So we can see how many
kilojoules of heat are lost.

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:10.255
So when that is happening, that tells
you that this is what you are trying to

00:07:10.255 --> 00:07:13.525
find, which is our Q value here, right?

00:07:13.525 --> 00:07:16.115
So Q, we're going to put a
little question mark next to it.

00:07:16.415 --> 00:07:18.295
Let us know this is what
we're trying to find.

00:07:18.955 --> 00:07:23.545
Now it says when the body temperature
of a surgery patient with a blood

00:07:23.545 --> 00:07:27.465
volume of 5500 milliliters is cooled.

00:07:27.805 --> 00:07:30.095
Okay, so now we have
another volume that's here.

00:07:30.374 --> 00:07:34.445
We have 5500 milliliters
of blood that is here.

00:07:34.739 --> 00:07:36.809
Blood is mainly made up of water.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:39.780
So we can assume that this is
the same equivalent as water.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.590
Um, we're using a health example
being that there's a lot of health

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:43.780
people that watch this as well.

00:07:44.269 --> 00:07:47.919
So we will have to use that
density there to convert to grams

00:07:47.939 --> 00:07:49.679
because we will need a mass.

00:07:49.919 --> 00:07:54.299
So maybe let's, before we get too
far into this, let's write our mass,

00:07:54.299 --> 00:08:04.460
our 5, 500 mLs, We can convert that
using the density that was given and

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:09.980
then we can see mLs cancels mLs and
this is equivalent to 5, 500 grams.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.979
All right, let's take a look at
what else is given in the problem.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:17.839
So the next thing that is
mentioned is that we had that

00:08:17.839 --> 00:08:20.580
this is being cooled from 38.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.219
5 degrees C to 33.

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.360
2 degrees C.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.780
So we have these two temperature values.

00:08:29.115 --> 00:08:30.665
that are right here in
the middle of the problem.

00:08:31.155 --> 00:08:36.204
Now, reading these careful is very,
very important because we need to make

00:08:36.204 --> 00:08:38.465
sure we are identifying them properly.

00:08:38.825 --> 00:08:43.015
So, we have TI, which is where
you're starting, your initial point.

00:08:43.564 --> 00:08:45.814
And this is referred to as 38.

00:08:45.854 --> 00:08:48.574
5 degrees C in the problem.

00:08:49.365 --> 00:08:54.815
And in the end, it says it goes down,
or we cool the patient down to 33.

00:08:54.915 --> 00:08:55.875
2 degrees C.

00:08:56.474 --> 00:09:00.194
So what we're going to have to
do is use this to get delta T.

00:09:00.595 --> 00:09:05.275
So being that we're going to be using
that MCAT equation from earlier,

00:09:05.824 --> 00:09:08.584
so delta T is final minus initial.

00:09:08.594 --> 00:09:11.545
So if we take, um, 33.

00:09:11.545 --> 00:09:14.704
2, minus it by 38.

00:09:14.705 --> 00:09:17.114
5, what we are going to get is 5.

00:09:17.244 --> 00:09:18.454
3 degrees C.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.080
when we do the final minus initial.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:27.110
Okay, now, now that we have all of
our pieces here, what we can now do,

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:30.759
and we also have our specific heat
as well, so I've already highlighted

00:09:30.759 --> 00:09:34.890
that earlier, we can plug in all
these pieces into our equation.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:37.790
So we're trying to find heat, right?

00:09:38.309 --> 00:09:41.950
We have our mass, which is 5500 grams.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:46.430
We are going to multiply that by
the specific heat, which is 4.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.340
186.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:49.300
Joules per grams by C.

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.350
So I'm going to highlight kind of
where all these are coming from.

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:56.300
So this, this first specific
heat is the blue value here.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:10:00.530
We have our mass that's
being placed in here.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.590
And then our last, last but not
least, we have our temperature,

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:07.009
which is at negative 5.

00:10:07.009 --> 00:10:07.780
3 degrees C.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.910
And we will highlight that as well,
we'll highlight that with purple.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:16.190
So, and let's move this over so that
