00:11:49.145 --> 00:11:51.694
Let's find out the identity
of an unknown metal.

00:11:52.055 --> 00:11:59.565
You found a 125 gram old cooking
pot and added 14, 600 joules of

00:11:59.565 --> 00:12:01.335
heat to raise the temperature.

00:12:02.229 --> 00:12:06.250
From 22 degrees C to 325 degrees C.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:09.439
What is the identity
of the old cooking pot?

00:12:09.449 --> 00:12:11.209
So you want to know what
is it made out of, right?

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.409
You want to know is it
something that's worth keeping?

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:17.019
So one thing that we're going to
do here is we're going to list

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.729
out all of our important values.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:23.340
So the first thing that we see is
that we have a mass of 125 grams.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:29.000
We have a heat value that is hidden
in this problem as well, right?

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:32.879
It's 14, 600, so that is a Q value.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:38.990
So 14, 600 JUULs, and we
have two temperature values.

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:49.600
So we have a TI of 22 degrees C, and
then we have a t F of 325 degrees C.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.560
So, and just to kind of highlight
where those two values came from, that

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.000
was from right here in the problem.

00:12:56.755 --> 00:12:59.345
Now that we have all these
different values, the one thing

00:12:59.345 --> 00:13:03.135
we got to see is, well, what are
we missing is our C value, right?

00:13:03.145 --> 00:13:06.355
So we want to figure out what the
identity is, and generally with these

00:13:06.365 --> 00:13:10.425
type of problems, you commonly see them
on exams when it comes to introductory

00:13:10.425 --> 00:13:15.355
chem, and we usually get a whole entire
list of different values that you can

00:13:15.355 --> 00:13:18.405
use here to try to identify what it is.

00:13:18.775 --> 00:13:22.055
Um, a lot of times this might be a
multiple choice question too, so maybe if

00:13:22.055 --> 00:13:25.445
you can take your luck at guessing, but
you should know how to do these, right?

00:13:25.445 --> 00:13:27.135
You want to get all those points.

00:13:27.715 --> 00:13:30.985
So if we have our Q equation,
what we will have to do is

00:13:31.005 --> 00:13:34.245
rearrange it to get C by itself.

00:13:34.824 --> 00:13:38.905
Now being that m, c, delta,
t are all being multiplied.

00:13:39.329 --> 00:13:46.479
What we can do is divide out m and delta
t to cancel them to get c by itself.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:51.620
So when we do that, we can see mass
cancels mass, and then delta t cancels

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:59.949
delta t, getting us our formula of
q m delta t is equal to c, okay?

00:14:00.519 --> 00:14:04.719
So now what we're going to do with
that equation is we're going to plug

00:14:04.729 --> 00:14:09.219
in all of the values that we were,
that we were given in the problem.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:13.230
So we can see that we
have our 14, 600 joules.

00:14:13.719 --> 00:14:19.580
We're going to be dividing that, um, times
our, our, dividing it by our mass, right?

00:14:19.979 --> 00:14:21.969
So that was 125 grams.

00:14:22.699 --> 00:14:28.610
And then we will also be dividing by delta
T, which is our final minus our initial.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:35.890
So we have our 325 degrees C, and
that's going to be minus 22 degrees C.

00:14:36.635 --> 00:14:41.289
Okay, so now, when we plug in all
these values, we have 14, 600.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:45.520
divided by, and one thing I always
recommend to all students is when

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:49.050
you're using your calculator, use
parentheses to your advantage so

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:52.980
you're not giving the wrong answers
when you are using your calculator.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:59.500
So it'll be divided by 125
times 325 minus 22 degrees C

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.130
when you are plugging that in.

